  "actions": "Enumerate the actual isolated Herdr keymap before launching the candidate under its host relay.\nDrive Ctrl+O twice, Ctrl+S idle, F1, F2 and Ctrl+G through the outer host input, then focus the KEYS explanation.\nRun an isolated host collision control that explicitly binds Ctrl+O.\nRead the frozen candidate release notes, docs/releases/v0.6.1.md lines30\u201336 and144\u2013147.",
  "expected": {
    "source": "case contract",
    "text": "The shipped footer is honest, chords reach Talaria, four tested defaults do not collide with host bindings, and F1/F2 behavior agrees with the KEYS explanation and notes."
  },
  "actual": "Nine actual foreground frame trios reviewed. Host noncollision is supported by43 live bindings and a44-binding positive control. Complete recorded gateway interval:66 consecutive frames,29 outgoing requests. This tests delivered terminal keys, not the macOS desktop setting itself. No claim of resistance to user-defined conflicting host bindings is made.\nClause 1: pass: The exact live footer names ctrl+o inspector, / commands, ctrl+s cancel-turn, ctrl+q quit and ctrl+g agents. It contains no F1/F2 eaten advisory. The configured Talaria keys are the shipped defaults. (https://github.com/infiquetra/talaria/issues/150#issuecomment-5562886840)\nClause 2: pass: Through the real nested host input path, Ctrl+O closes and reopens Inspector in the same recorded session. The open, closed and reopened bound frames witness the effect. (https://github.com/infiquetra/talaria/issues/150#issuecomment-5562886840)\nClause 3: pass: Ctrl+S in the foreground produces the complete notice: nothing to interrupt \u2014 no turn is in flight. Talaria remains running and responds to subsequent input. (https://github.com/infiquetra/talaria/issues/150#issuecomment-5562886840)\nClause 4: pass: The same live host used for every frame has43 enumerated bindings: its complete scrolled key-help inventory plus four active pane-swap bindings omitted by that help but explicit in its unchanged launch configuration. Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, F1 and F2 are all absent. A separate isolated positive control with a direct Ctrl+O binding yields44 bindings and detects Ctrl+O; the control file is listed separately. Both files contain keys and action labels only. (https://github.com/infiquetra/talaria/issues/150#issuecomment-5562886840)\nClause 5: pass: F1 leaves the full captured cell frame unchanged; the before and after frames agree and its absence from the binding inventory supports that observation. F2 displays no sub-agents to show or hide \u2014 the region stays hidden. After a real focus change resets the documented notice latch, Ctrl+G independently displays the same notice. The focused KEYS row explains F1, F2 and the macOS standard-function-key setting in full. Frozen release notes lines30\u201336 describe those same semantics and setting. (https://github.com/infiquetra/talaria/issues/150#issuecomment-5562886840)",
